From 03c9b2cacd41f9bd1e5f30423b40ca2a21bb45ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:08:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] grate: store and sample linear mip chains without
 texture aborts

Allocate real mip levels and use their pitches and offsets for maps,
copies, clears, render targets and blits. Program mip filtering and LOD
bounds using NVIDIA's T30 layout and sampler encoding. Handle mirrored
repeat, repack non-native imported strides, and reject unsupported views
without aborting.

Checked against original NVIDIA ARM replay: 63 resource cases and 328
exact descriptor matches. Tegra passes 219 mipmap cases and all nine
wrap combinations. The full suite has 27 successful tests and one
expected skip; interleaved benchmarks show no material slowdown.
